#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:77
msgid ""
"Rewrites each ``while cond: BODY`` into a bounded serial ``for`` loop "
"(tagged ``synthetic_while``) so AutoSchedule can pipeline the body, then "
"extracts complex ``if`` conditions and buffer-dependent serial/unrolled loop "
"bounds into temporary ``Bind`` variables. :func:`RestoreWhileLoops` undoes "
"the while-rewrite after scheduling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:93
msgid ""
"Requires :func:`NormalizeControlFlowForSchedule` followed "
"by :func:`MaterializeScheduleUnits`, so buffer-dependent control expressions "
"are schedulable tasks and manual stages and flattened scheduling guards are "
"available through the shared IRStructure codec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:123
msgid ""
"This pre-AutoSchedule pass only materializes ``T.unroll(..., "
"explicit=True)`` loops. Non-explicit unroll hints, serial loops, and all VF "
"block interiors are preserved for their later lowering stages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:127
msgid ""
"Each cloned VMI allocation gets a fresh data Var, and the corresponding "
"``tl.vmi.alloc_kind`` AttrStmt carrier emitted by "
"``NormalizePTOAllocMarkers`` is remapped to that Var through the same "
"mapping used for buffer loads and stores.  A carrier whose allocation was "
"not rebuilt by the clone keeps its original Var."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:138
msgid ""
"Consumes each SBlock's ``tl.vmi.alloc_kind`` map and emits one "
"``AttrStmt(data_var, \"tl.vmi.alloc_kind\", StringImm(kind))`` per marked "
"allocation in the block that actually owns it, in ``alloc_buffers`` order. "
"Carriers for a ``SIMD_VF`` block go inside its existing outer "
"``tl.simdvf_scope`` statement; carriers for a nested block go in that "
"block's body.  Allocations, data Vars, statement order, and unrelated "
"annotations stay untouched, and marked allocations owned outside a "
"``SIMD_VF`` are rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:147
msgid ""
"The pass is idempotent: existing carriers and final allocation annotations "
"are not duplicated.  Run it after binding the Ascend PTO target and before "
"``UnrollLoopSkipVF``.  Functions without a PTO target pass through unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:157
msgid ""
"Must run immediately after ``LowerOpaqueBlock`` on the PTO target.  It "
"collects the temporary ``tl.vmi.alloc_kind`` AttrStmt carriers and the "
"actual ``AllocBuffer`` statements before rewriting, matches them by data Var "
"identity, writes the kind to the matched allocation's annotations, and "
"removes the consumed carriers while preserving their bodies and order. An "
"orphan carrier or conflicting kinds are rejected.  The final allocation need "
"not be lexically inside ``tl.simdvf_scope``, because lowering materializes "
"it before the scope statement.  Functions without a PTO target pass through "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:172
msgid ""
"Every ordinary ``T.vmi.vload`` / ``T.vmi.vstore`` address (a scalar-origin "
"``BufferLoad``) is replaced with ``tl.access_ptr(BufferLoad, extent, "
"rw_mask)`` plus a rewritten instruction scalar offset.  The pass proves, in "
"one shared acceptance exit, that the descriptor preserves the source "
"address, contains the complete physical access envelope and covers the "
"declared extent under the existing logical pointer-region analysis.  An "
"ordinary caller-written explicit descriptor is preserved and only verified; "
"there is no whole-allocation fallback for an ordinary access.  Indexed "
"``vgather`` / ``vscatter`` addresses, including one reached through a direct "
"handle binding, are instead rebuilt as an owner-origin descriptor with "
"capacity ``prod(owner.shape)`` after the owner identity, layout, capacity, "
"stable-coverage and bound-address snapshot proofs. Functions without a PTO "
"target pass through unchanged; the pass is a no-op on IR without VMI "
"accesses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:252
msgid ""
"Runs on the PTO target only: SIMD_VF blocks whose T.Parallel units fall "
"outside the supported mapping contract are rejected, while functions without "
"a PTO target pass through unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:261
msgid ""
"Only the registration exists for now, so that the formal PTO pipeline order "
"is fixed; the safe scalar If/Select/Min/Max rewrites are left to a later "
"change. The placeholder preserves the input IR and rejects nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:271
msgid ""
"Consumes the final device TIR after LowerDeviceKernelLaunch and the final "
"layout and UB rewrites. Currently checks destination alignment for default/"
"continuous explicit-mask VMI stores of b8/b16/b32 data: 32 bytes for "
"ordinary stores, or natural element alignment for recognized 1PT writeback. "
"Bool data is excluded. Shapes, layouts, masks and addresses are unchanged. "
"Functions without a PTO target pass through unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:281
msgid ""
"Rewrite verified T.Parallel loops inside PTO SIMD_VF blocks into logical VMI "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/transform/index.rst:284
msgid ""
"Runs on the PTO target only; functions without a PTO target pass through "
"unchanged."
msgstr ""

